ycle","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A cycle: a closed path, at least one edge long, listed without repeating its start (NetworkX’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"simple_cycles","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", petgraph). Vertex i goes to vertex (i + 1) mod "},{"code":"count","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" through edge i, and no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex or edge position appears twice; a self-loop is a cycle of length 1, two parallel edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one of length 2. It is the witness cycle detection returns."}]},"doc://Tours/documentation/Tours":{"url":"\/documentation\/tours","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[],"title":"Tours","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours","kind":"symbol"}}}